    "text": "A concave mirror has radius of curvature of <math><mn>40</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math> It is at the bottom of a glass that has water filled up to <math><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> (see figure). If a small particle is floating on the surface of water, its image as seen, from directly above the glass, is at a distance <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> from the surface of water. The value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> is close to: (Refractive index of water <math><mo>=</mo><mn>1.33</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0178_50167c735b8f.png\" style=\"width: 201px; height: 194px;\" />"
